# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bluespec / Bluesim build artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build_bsim/
build_v/
verilog_dir/

*.bo
*.ba
*.so

# linked simulator executables (TOPMODULE is mkTest, so mkTest_bsim*)
mkTest_bsim
mkTest_bsim.so
*_bsim
*_vsim
out
out.so

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Waveform dumps
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated by the -V flag on every saved run. 664 of these came to 2.2 GB,
# which is well past what GitHub will take. Regenerate any one of them with
# the 'reproduce' line in that run's config.txt.
*.vcd

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Active RTL working copy
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# run_sspi_tb.sh --rtl copies the chosen variant over rtl/sspi.bsv, because
# that is the only filename bsc resolves 'import sspi' to. Its content is just
# whichever variant ran last, so it is not a source file. The named variants
# in rtl/ are the real artifacts.
#
# NOTE: a fresh clone therefore has no rtl/sspi.bsv. Pick a variant on the
# first run, e.g. --rtl sspi_setup_rx_no_edge_rx.bsv
rtl/sspi.bsv
rtl/sspi.bsv.prev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated testbench input
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Written by run_sspi_tb.sh --data. Only included by the testbenches when
# TB_DATA_FILE is defined, so its absence is harmless.
sspi_tb_data.bsvi

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
